# ESP32 Embedded Engineering

- Read the repository root `AGENTS.md` before making changes.
- The canonical task-specific knowledge lives in `skills/<id>/SKILL.md`.
  Search for the skill matching the failure mode, not just the component name.
- Identify exact SoC, module, board revision, framework/version and toolchain
  before making hardware-sensitive recommendations.
- Run relevant checkers from `tools/` before code changes and before flashing.
- Treat datasheets, errata, schematics and version-matched official docs as
  primary evidence. Preserve uncertainty and issue status.
- Never disable brownout detection to hide a power-integrity fault.
- Never imply an ESP32 is a safety-rated controller.
- Distinguish software/CI success from physical hardware validation.
- See `rules/common/agent-workflow.md` and
  `rules/embedded/hardware-safety.md` for the full workflow.
